// SyncTransactions: Sync transactions (change feed).
//
// Returns what changed in a connection's transactions since a `cursor`:
// `added`, `modified` and `removed` (with a `reason`), across all its accounts.
// An empty cursor returns every current transaction as `added` and sets `reset:
// true`: replace your copy with it instead of adding to it.
//
// The first read is a true snapshot. A first read (no cursor, or the read after
// `reset`) returns every transaction the connection had when the read started,
// each exactly once as `added`, in its current state, even if a sync runs while
// you page. Changes made while you were paging arrive in the next read from
// `next_cursor`: a transaction you already received comes again as `modified`,
// and a new one as `added`. Apply `modified` as an upsert by `id`, and ignore a
// `removed` id you do not have. All pages of one read reflect the same point in
// time. Keep paging with `page_token` while `has_more` is `true`, and store
// `next_cursor` only after a response with `has_more: false`. If paging fails
// midway, restart from the cursor you had stored.
//
// The change log is replayable for 90 days. An older cursor answers `410
// cursor_expired` with `bootstrap: true`: start again from an empty cursor.
// Stored history is never aged out while the connection exists. A booked
// pending transaction appears in `added` and the pending one in `removed` with
// `reason: pending_booked`. Webhook `bank.data.updated` tells you when to call.
//
// Needs an API key with the Bank data permission (`bank-data`): read for this
// operation. A key with full access does not include it: grant it explicitly
// when you create the key, or the call answers `403 bank_data_access_denied`. A
// sandbox application reads its Test Bank data with the key alone. A request
// without an API key (client credentials) is refused on raw data with the same
// `403`.
//
//	GET /v3/bank/connections/{id}/transactions/sync/
func (r *BankService) SyncTransactions(ctx context.Context, id string, params BankSyncTransactionsParams, opts ...option.RequestOption) (*BankTransactionChanges, error) {
	res := new(BankTransactionChanges)
	if _, err := r.client.do(ctx, &apiRequest{method: http.MethodGet, path: "/v3/bank/connections/{id}/transactions/sync/", pathParams: []string{"id", id}, params: params}, res, opts); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return res, nil
}

